    {
      "id": "p016",
      "text": "Observe, that the nose has been formed to bear\nspectacles--thus we have spectacles. Legs are visibly designed for\nstockings--and we have stockings.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p005",
      "replacements": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p017",
      "text": "Stones were made to be hewn, and to\nconstruct castles--therefore my lord has a magnificent castle; for the\ngreatest baron in the province ought to be the best lodged. Pigs were\nmade to be eaten--therefore we eat pork all the year round. Consequently\nthey who assert that all is well have said a foolish thing, they should\nhave said all is for the best.\"",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p005",
      "replacements": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p018",
      "text": "Candide listened attentively and believed innocently; for he thought\nMiss Cunegonde extremely beautiful, though he never had the courage to\ntell her so.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p006",
      "replacements": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p019",
      "text": "He concluded that after the happiness of being born of\nBaron of Thunder-ten-Tronckh, the second degree of happiness was to be\nMiss Cunegonde, the third that of seeing her every day, and the fourth\nthat of hearing Master Pangloss, the greatest philosopher of the whole\nprovince, and consequently of the whole world.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p006",
      "replacements": [
